<li><a id="n6"></a>Annette Vissing-Jorgensen,<a href="https://www.ecb.europa.eu/press/conferences/ecbforum/shared/pdf/2023/VissingJorgensen_paper.pdf" target="_blank"> &ldquo;Balance Sheet Policy Above the  ELB,&rdquo;</a> remarks at the  European Central Bank Forum on Central Banking, June 26&ndash;28, 2023. </li>
<li><a id="n7"></a>In the Federal Reserve&rsquo;s March 2024 <a href="https://www.federalreserve.gov/data/sfos/march-2024-senior-financial-officer-survey.htm" target="_blank">Senior Financial Officer Survey,</a> the median domestic bank respondent  said it would not lend federal funds overnight for less than a 25-basis-point  spread over interest on reserves. See also Kyungmin Kim, Antoine Martin and Ed  Nosal, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1111/jmcb.12693" target="_blank">&ldquo;Can the U.S. Interbank Market Be  Revived?&rdquo; </a> <em>Journal  of Money, Credit and Banking</em> 52(7), 1645-1689, October 2020.</li>
<li><a id="n8"></a>See, for example, Simon Potter, <a href="https://www.newyorkfed.org/newsevents/speeches/2017/pot170405" target="_blank">&ldquo;Money Markets at a Crossroads:  Policy Implementation at a Time of Structural Change,&rdquo;</a> remarks at the Master of Applied  Economics&rsquo; Distinguished Speaker Series, University of California, Los Angeles,  April 5, 2017. </li>
<li><a id="n9"></a>Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System,  &ldquo;Request for Information and Comment on Operational Aspects of Federal Reserve  Bank Extensions of Discount Window and Intraday Credit,&rdquo; <em>Federal Register</em> 89(175), 73415-73418.</li>
<li><a id="n10"></a>Federal Reserve  Bank of New York, <a href="https://www.newyorkfed.org/markets/opolicy/operating_policy_250220" target="_blank">&ldquo;Statement  Regarding Repurchase Agreement Small Value Exercise,&rdquo;</a> February 20,  2025. </li>
<li><a id="n11"></a>See, for example, James A. Clouse, Sebastian Infante,  and Zeynep Senyuz, <a href="https://www.federalreserve.gov/econres/notes/feds-notes/market-based-indicators-on-the-road-to-ample-reserves-20250131.html" target="_blank">&ldquo;Market-Based Indicators on the Road  to Ample Reserves,&rdquo;</a> <em>FEDS  Notes</em>, Jan. 31, 2025.</li>
<li><a id="n12"></a>Elsewhere, I have discussed which money market rates  I am watching most closely to assess liquidity conditions. The secured  overnight financing rate, while an important reference rate, includes some  transactions whose rates reflect compensation for intermediating funds from the  triparty segment of the repo market to cash borrowers who lack triparty access. For this reason, I believe the somewhat narrower tri-party general collateral  rate currently provides a cleaner read on liquidity conditions in U.S. secured  markets. See Lorie K. Logan, <a href="/news/speeches/logan/2024/lkl241021">&ldquo;Normalizing the FOMC&rsquo;s monetary  policy tools,&rdquo;</a> remarks at the Securities Industry and Financial Markets Association annual  meeting, Oct. 21, 2024.  </li>
<li><a id="n13"></a>Federal Open Market Committee, <a href="https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressreleases/monetary20220126c.htm" target="_blank">&ldquo;Principles for Reducing the Size of  the Federal Reserve&rsquo;s Balance Sheet,&rdquo;</a> Jan. 26, 2022.</li>
<li><a id="n14"></a>Such an offering would be similar to the Federal  Reserve&rsquo;s Term Auction Facility, which offered term discount window loans at an  auction rate in 2007 through 2010. 
